# Try-it playground for #104, the strict only filter "!!".
#
# A 3 x 3 grid of items, rows A, B, C and columns 1, 2, 3, laid out
# top-down ("style vertical"). The column flows (A1 -> B1 -> C1, ...)
# are constrained and give the rows; the row flows (A1 -> A2 -> A3, ...)
# and the two diagonals are relaxed ("->?", "--?") so that they do not
# shift the grid. Once a filter applies, the rest is no longer a grid.
# Flows are labelled "source dest" in lowercase. Z is a spare item for
# the replacement-group variants.
#
# At the end, a menu of filter blocks: exactly one block is active;
# comment it out, uncomment another one, then render:
#
#     ./data-flow-diagram devlog/104-try-it.dfd && xdg-open devlog/104-try-it.svg
#
# Vocabulary: a filter's path flows are the flows it followed to reach
# its neighbors; the stray flows are the other flows between kept items.
# "!!" keeps the same items as "!" but hides the stray flows at the
# items it selects. A plain "!" naming both ends of a flow shows it
# regardless; a path flow of any "!!" is always shown.

style vertical

process A1
process A2
process A3
process B1
process B2
process B3
process C1
process C2
process C3
process Z Group

# columns: vertical flows, they lay out the rows (top to bottom)
A1 -> B1 a1b1
B1 -> C1 b1c1
A2 -> B2 a2b2
B2 -> C2 b2c2
A3 -> B3 a3b3
B3 -> C3 b3c3

# rows: horizontal flows, relaxed so that they do not shift the grid
A1 ->? A2 a1a2
A2 ->? A3 a2a3
B1 ->? B2 b1b2
B2 ->? B3 b2b3
C1 ->? C2 c1c2
C2 ->? C3 c2c3

A1 ->? B2 a1b2
B1 --? C2 b1c2

####### ############### ###############################
# Filter menu: one block active at a time

##### A. Plain: A1 and two levels downstream, all flows among them.
# 8 items (all but C3), 12 flows. Baseline for B and C.
!>2 A1

##### B. Strict: the same 8 items, only the path flows: 10 flows. The
# two stray flows a3b3 and c1c2 are hidden: A3, B3, C1, C2 are kept (two
# flows from A1) but these flows lie on no path from A1 of two flows.
#!!>2 A1

##### C. Strict, then a plain "!" naming both ends of a stray flow:
# c1c2 is back (11 flows); a3b3 stays hidden.
#!!>2 A1
#! C1 C2

##### D. Two strict filters compose: A1 one flow downstream (A2, B1, B2)
# and C2 one flow upstream (B2, C1, B1). 6 items, 6 flows: the path
# flows a1a2, a1b1, a1b2 of the first and b2c2, c1c2, b1c2 of the
# second. Hidden strays: a2b2, b1c1, b1b2, each touching a strict
# selection and on no path, although both their ends are kept.
#!!>1 A1
#!!<1 C2

##### E. Strict, then a plain "!" with neighbors: the plain neighborhood
# of B3 (A3, B2, C3) shows all its flows, so a3b3 is back and b3c3 comes
# in with C3. 9 items, 12 flows; c1c2 stays hidden.
#!!>2 A1
#!<>1 B3

##### F. Plain, then a replacement group: row B collapses into Z. Items
# A1 A2 A3 C1 C2 Z; 10 flows, among them a3b3 rewired to A3 -> Z and
# c1c2. The filter comes first, as in the doc's group example
# (§ 7.4.2.2): the selection is made on the original flows, then the
# group is formed; Z, an anchor without flows at that point, brings
# nothing but itself. See block J for the reversed order.
#!>2 A1 Z
#~=Z B1 B2 B3

##### G. Strict, then the same replacement group: 8 flows. The rewired
# stray a3b3 (A3 -> Z) and c1c2 are hidden; the rewired path flows
# stay: path membership survives the rewiring. Compare with F.
#!!>2 A1 Z
#~=Z B1 B2 B3

##### H. The crossed pattern: a1a2 and b1b2 wanted, a1b1, a2b2 and a1b2
# not, all four items kept. A span-less strict filter hides every flow
# touching the four items, then one plain "!" per wanted pair shows it.
# 4 items, 2 flows.
#!! A1 A2 B1 B2
#! A1 A2
#! B1 B2

##### I. Strict, then a plain removal: "~" removes A3 and C1 with their
# flows, as always. 6 items, 8 flows.
#!!>2 A1
#~ A3 C1

##### J. The reversed group order, TODO item 23, not a strict-filter
# case. Declaring the group first reads naturally but does not work
# today: a "~" as first filter starts from the full set, so the "!" that
# follows narrows nothing (C3 stays), and the traversal from A1 reads
# the original flows, so B1, B2, B3 come back as orphans next to Z.
# 10 items, 12 flows. Expected once fixed: recorded in TODO item 23.
#~=Z B1 B2 B3
#!>2 A1 Z

##### K. The crossed pattern by paths, no plain pair: two strict filters
# with span 1. "!!<1 A2" selects A1 through a1a2; "!!>1 B1" selects B2,
# C1, C2 through b1b2, b1c1, b1c2. The flows a1b1, a2b2 and a1b2 join
# kept items but touch a selection and are on no path: hidden. 6 items,
# 4 flows.
#!!<1 A2
#!!>1 B1

##### L. K plus a plain pair: a1b1 is back; a2b2 and a1b2 stay hidden.
# 5 flows.
#!!<1 A2
#!!>1 B1
#! A1 B1
